  "extraction_notes": "The table shows a generic transformation 7→8 plus nine specific examples 8a–8i. Reagent 1 was identified from the drawn catalyst as bis(2-chlorophenyl)borinic acid. For entry 7, the substrate corresponding to proline methyl ester is inferred from product 8g; the table only explicitly draws the product, so the reactant structure is assigned as the corresponding secondary amine substrate. Entry 8 side chain is read as BocHN(CH2)3– attached to the α-carbon (ornithine-derived methyl ester). Absolute stereochemistry follows the wedges as drawn, but amino ester starting materials are not named with D/L descriptors in the figure."
